+# CONTRACT — Versioned Document Store with Structural Merge
+
+Definition of done. Every box must be verified by a test in `tests/`.
+
+## Documents (CRUD)
+- [ ] `create(id, content)` stores a new document → get(id) returns deep-equal content
+- [ ] `create` throws if id already exists on current branch
+- [ ] `create` deep-clones input (mutating the input object afterward does not change stored content)
+- [ ] `get(id)` returns current content → deep-equal to last written
+- [ ] `get` returns a deep clone (mutating the returned object does not change stored content)
+- [ ] `get` throws if document does not exist
+- [ ] `get` throws if document was deleted
+- [ ] `update(id, content)` replaces content + creates a new version → get reflects new content
+- [ ] `update` throws if document does not exist
+- [ ] `update` deep-clones input
+- [ ] `delete(id)` removes a document from current branch → get throws afterward
+- [ ] `delete` throws if document does not exist
+- [ ] document can be re-created after delete
+
+## Version History
+- [ ] every `create` produces a version
+- [ ] every `update` produces a new version
+- [ ] `getHistory(id)` returns versions chronologically (oldest first)
+- [ ] each Version has unique `id`, numeric `timestamp`, and full `content` at that point
+- [ ] version contents are clones (mutating a returned version content does not affect store)
+- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns content at that version
+- [ ] `getVersion` throws for unknown version
+
+## Branching
+- [ ] default branch is `"main"` → getBranch() === "main"
+- [ ] `createBranch(name)` branches from current branch's current state
+- [ ] `createBranch(name, fromBranch)` branches from the given branch
+- [ ] `createBranch` throws if branch name already exists
+- [ ] `switchBranch(name)` changes active branch → getBranch() reflects it
+- [ ] `switchBranch` throws for unknown branch
+- [ ] `listBranches()` lists all branch names (includes main)
+- [ ] changes on one branch are not visible on another branch
+- [ ] a doc created before branching is visible on the new branch
+- [ ] a doc created after branching on parent is NOT on the earlier-made child
+
+## Merging (three-way)
+- [ ] merge with no changes on either side → applied: true, no conflicts (no-op / fast-forward)
+- [ ] field changed only on source → taken, no conflict, applied
+- [ ] field changed only on current (ours) → kept, no conflict
+- [ ] same field changed to SAME value on both → no conflict
+- [ ] same field changed to DIFFERENT values on both → conflict reported
+- [ ] conflict reported with correct documentId, dot-path, base, ours, theirs
+- [ ] nested field conflict reports nested dot-path (e.g. "a.b.c")
+- [ ] when conflicts exist → applied: false AND current branch unchanged
+- [ ] when conflicts exist → merged still contains result with ours preferred at conflict
+- [ ] when no conflicts → merge auto-applied to current branch (get reflects merged)
+- [ ] document created only on source → appears in merged, taken
+- [ ] document created only on ours → preserved
+- [ ] changes to DIFFERENT documents on different branches merge with no conflict
+- [ ] changes to DIFFERENT fields of the SAME document merge with no conflict
+- [ ] deletion on one side, unchanged on other → document removed, no conflict
+- [ ] deletion on one side, modified on other → conflict (delete/modify)
+- [ ] array field treated as a leaf value (different arrays → conflict, not element merge)
+- [ ] merged field maps documentId -> merged content (resulting state)
+- [ ] applied merge creates versions on current branch (history updated)
+- [ ] re-merging same source after a clean merge is a no-op (no spurious conflicts)
+
+## Build / Lint
+- [ ] `npm run build` succeeds (tsc clean)
+- [ ] `npm run lint` succeeds (eslint clean)
+- [ ] `npm test` all green
